{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Field-wide pattern (June 2026): every agent-memory product gates quality at WRITE time with an LLM judge, and handles decay REACTIVELY — a fact only goes stale when a contradicting fact arrives (bi-temporal valid_at/invalid_at + created_at/expired_at). Even Zep/Graphiti, the gold standard, has NO proactive staleness sweep (confirmed in paper + issues): a stale-but-uncontradicted fact lives forever.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Decay camp 1 (reactive / bi-temporal): Zep/Graphiti, Mem0-g (soft-invalidate), Cognee (versioning), zonoid. New contradicting fact closes the old fact's validity window; old fact retained, never deleted. Precise/auditable/supports as-of queries. Limitation: only fires on contradiction.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Decay camp 2 (proactive / forgetting-curve): FadeMem (dual Weibull curves), YourMemory (Ebbinghaus + recall boost), MemoryBank, MemoryOS (heat score), SSGM (theoretical). Score decays with time/disuse, prune below threshold, recall reinforces. Bounds graph growth but BLIND TO TRUTH — prunes valid-but-rarely-accessed facts; MemoryBank performs worst in its own benchmark. Almost nobody combines camp 1 + camp 2.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Other decay handling: Letta/MemGPT + MemOS = eviction/lifecycle (FIFO + recursive summarization; state machine Generated→…→Expired) with no importance weighting (drops oldest regardless of value). Mem0/Glean = re-rank only (recent access 1.5x, unused 0.3x; nothing deleted → stale facts resurface). A-MEM/Memary/LangMem/all GraphRAG-family = NO decay (timestamps stored but never used to prune; logically-stale edges persist forever).","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Quality-gate dominant pattern = Mem0 AUDN: per fact, an LLM picks ADD/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP against top-k similar memories. Core flaw shared by Mem0/FadeMem/Zep: the SAME model extracts AND judges → correlated failure (the judge inherits the extractor's hallucination).","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Quality-gate variants: Zep bi-temporal contradiction check (no confidence floor — any non-duplicate fact enters); FadeMem 4-way conflict classes (Compatible/Contradictory/Subsumptive/Subsumed); DEG-RAG LLM judge on 5 criteria dropping triples <0.2 (dropped ~40% of triples, lifted LightRAG win-rate 42%→58%); RGMem corroboration threshold θ_inf=3 (don't update memory until ≥3 episodes corroborate); SSGM NLI verify-before-write; traceable-validation RAG-over-Wikipedia (88% precision but only 44% recall).","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"PRODUCTION VALIDATION that unjudged automatic memory accretion fails: Cursor REMOVED its Memories feature in 2.1.x and told users to convert to manually-authored Rules. ChatGPT memory was 41.5% factually accurate in 2024, fixed only by adding a background-synthesis pass ('Dreaming') → 82.8% — i.e. they had to bolt on a judging/consolidation loop after the fact. Both confirm the recorded thesis: the judging loop, not the memory, is the moat.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","item":"Borrowable gaps for zonoid (priority order): (1) DECAY ON USEFULNESS not age — biggest unrealized edge; feed the recall-outcome journal into a graded decay/confidence score (reinforce notes that pay off, decay never-recalled-and-helpful), bridging the reactive + forgetting-curve camps without the latter's 'kills valid-but-quiet facts' downside; natural home = stale_flags in the KB-learner run record; THIS IS task #1 (note-decay). (2) corroboration threshold (RGMem θ_inf) before a curious_candidate becomes inject-eligible. (3) scalar confidence floor (DEG-RAG) for a graded inject gate vs the current ~binary judge. (4) subsumption not just supersession (FadeMem): handle 'new note more specific/general than existing' → merge/refine. DO NOT copy: time-based TTL / decay-by-deletion — keep the bi-temporal close-window-never-delete approach (strictly safer for auditability + as-of).","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.956Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgrel2bjak","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Competitive position vs agent memory products: outcome-grounded judging is the unique edge; decay-on-usefulness is the top gap","summary":"Cross-competitor synthesis (extends survey note-mqgqarwuqkz) on knowledge decay + low-quality-write handling across agent-memory products. HEADLINE: the whole field gates quality at WRITE time with an LLM judge and handles decay only REACTIVELY — a fact goes stale only when a contradicting fact arrives; even Zep/Graphiti (gold standard) has NO proactive staleness sweep. zonoid is at PARITY with Zep on the bi-temporal/structural axis (validFrom/validTo + supersedes chains + as-of retrieval) and genuinely AHEAD on quality — the only design that ALSO judges on downstream OUTCOME, not just at ingestion. Three things no competitor combines: (1) a SEPARATE adversarial judge (not the extractor judging itself → defeats the correlated-failure flaw in Mem0/FadeMem/Zep where one model both writes and gates); (2) OUTCOME-grounded quality via the recall-outcome attribution seam (did the note actually make a downstream task cheaper/succeed — post-hoc ground truth the write-time judges structurally cannot access); (3) the empirical/non-derivable content bar (structurally excludes the derivable noise that clogged Cursor/ChatGPT memories). PRODUCTION VALIDATION of the 'judging loop is the moat' thesis: Cursor REMOVED its Memories feature in 2.1.x (→ manual Rules); ChatGPT memory was 41.5% factually accurate in 2024, fixed only by bolting on a background-synthesis 'Dreaming' pass → 82.8%. TOP UNREALIZED EDGE: decay on USEFULNESS not age — feed recall-outcome into a graded decay/confidence score (reinforce on payoff, decay on never-recalled-and-helpful), bridging the reactive and forgetting-curve camps without the latter's 'kills valid-but-quiet facts' downside; this is exactly task #1 (note-decay). ONE-LINE POSITION: everyone gates at the door with the same LLM that wrote it and forgets only when contradicted; zonoid gates with an independent judge, keeps only empirically-discovered knowledge, and re-grades notes by whether they paid off downstream — Cursor's and ChatGPT's memory fai","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T14:50:39.779Z","vec":[-0.04957794398069382,-0.001554936752654612,-0.07160980254411697,-0.001598962931893766,0.024879811331629753,-0.02452804706990719,-0.03598431125283241,0.08372614532709122,0.04090607911348343,0.053017012774944305,-0.014259584248065948,0.02450690045952797,0.07378622889518738,-0.007928204722702503,-0.03870171681046486,0.04820942133665085,0.09534314274787903,0.038966383785009384,-0.10275162011384964,-0.005783081986010075,0.031524334102869034,-0.035518430173397064,0.026872646063566208,-0.019001608714461327,-0.0810319110751152,-0.007485692854970694,-0.10655257105827332,-0.009574031457304955,-0.004088391549885273,-0.1093905046582222,0.007136142812669277,0.12484627217054367,0.005037170834839344,-0.010112299583852291,-0.06318390369415283,0.050095248967409134,-0.04193612188100815,0.0033096729312092066,-0.01852031797170639,-0.06007399037480354,0.02989201433956623,0.057467248290777206,-0.08260311186313629,-0.02805395983159542,0.058989688754081726,-0.005946983117610216,-0.028501104563474655,-0.04399598762392998,-0.13971605896949768,0.013980437070131302,-0.10478147119283676,0.023926399648189545,-0.024190498515963554,0.10674852877855301,0.007333665154874325,0.10780423134565353,0.03953957185149193,0.05980648100376129,-0.0976325124502182,-0.030597278848290443,0.006148235406726599,-0.0734855979681015,-0.08924322575330734,-0.04890837147831917,0.019770976155996323,-0.015458149835467339,0.040399275720119476,0.005493541248142719,-0.004067470785230398,-0.006384373176842928,0.022090991958975792,-0.004235442262142897,-0.06414839625358582,-0.022406205534934998,0.004677880089730024,0.07456795126199722,0.044788528233766556,-0.03814518824219704,0.04266033694148064,-0.08450188487768173,-0.011236642487347126,0.00390